.TH SDL_WaitProcess 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_WaitProcess \- Wait for a process to finish.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_process.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_WaitProcess(SDL_Process *process, bool block, int *exitcode);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This can be called multiple times to get the status of a process\[char46]
.PP
The exit code will be the exit code of the process if it terminates normally, a negative signal if it terminated due to a signal, or -255 otherwise\[char46] It will not be changed if the process is still running\[char46]
.PP
If you create a process with standard output piped to the application
.BR "" ( pipe_stdio
being true) then you should read all of the process output before calling
.BR SDL_WaitProcess ()\[char46]
If you don\(aqt do this the process might be blocked indefinitely waiting for output to be read and
.BR SDL_WaitProcess ()
will never return true;

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I process
The process to wait for\[char46]
.TP
.I block
If true, block until the process finishes; otherwise, report on the process\(aq status\[char46]
.TP
.I exitcode
a pointer filled in with the process exit code if the process has exited, may be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if the process exited, false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function is not thread safe\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

